     "text": "```json\n{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"Exfiltration needs admin on db, fileserver or backup. Each of these first needs a foothold from auth_db, auth_fileserver or auth_backup. Those require (NOT mfa_dbadmin OR admin_dc OR admin_adfs). mfa_dbadmin is deployed, so the attacker would need admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those require foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, which come only from auth_dc and auth_adfs. Both require NOT mfa_admin, and mfa_admin is deployed. The attacker can still go far: exploit_web, then pivot_internal (no segmentation), steal_user_cred, auth to the app, API or CI server (no user MFA), kerberoast for stolen_admin, and escalate_ciserver then leak_secrets for stolen_dbadmin. But the db, fileserver and backup auth steps stay blocked, so exfiltrated cannot be reached.\"}\n```"
